00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,260
That is why the number is higher,

00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:36,260
say with a CD3 to CD16 ratio.

00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:40,760
Yes, so when you look at that's the problem,

00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:45,760
when you look at a differentiation,

00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:49,760
usually if you do CBC with a differential,

00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,260
it's only going to measure neutrophils.

00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,260
The differential is breaking down to the white blood cells

00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:58,260
into lymphocytes, neutrophils, monocytes, blah, blah, blah.

00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:02,260
It's not going to break it down deeper into NK cells,

00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:04,760
which are natural killer cells,

00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:09,260
and all the other CD cell line,

00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:11,760
unless you do a deep dive in it.

00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,260
There's argument whether the deep dive

00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,260
with a value of the deep dive.

00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:23,260
I don't recommend it even though one of the best tests for that is a Syrex.

00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:26,260
I forgot what it is, Ray 23, I think it is.

